<title>FRANCE: RHONE-POULENC SLIPS ON BID OUTLOOK.</title>
<headline>RHONE-POULENC SLIPS ON BID OUTLOOK.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Rhone-Poulenc slipped on expectations it may have to increase its pending bid for minorities in Rhone-Poulenc Rorer from the expected $92 per share.</p>
<p>Dealers said there was talk in the market the bid had to be raised to $100 to $110 per share to be succesful. Rhone has 68 percent in Rorer.</p>
<p>The share was also affected by the dilution of its capital. It created 4.7 million new shares and increased the capital to 807 million francs due to a share alternative for the dividend payment.</p>
<p>At 1030 GMT, Rhone was down 1.62 percent at 255.50 francs while the CAC-40 index was up 0.56 percent at 3054.14.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
